Texas Railroad Commission public records
----------------------------------------

The paths below are derived from public records of the Railroad Commission
of Texas (RRC): one night's Drilling Permit (W-1) imaged files, the Drilling
Permit Master daily file (daf420.dat), and the RRC record-layout manual
OGA049M. They remain under the RRC's terms. They are excluded from the MIT
License, and the MIT grant in LICENSE does not apply to them.

The terms as recorded when the files were fetched (corpus/manifest.json,
line 7): "Texas public record (Tex. Gov't Code ch. 552); RRC data sets
published free of charge; site policy: copy for noncommercial use,
unaltered". Check the RRC's current terms before any reuse.

1. corpus/manifest.json
   Source URLs, hashes, page counts, and class labels of the RRC files.
   Evidence, corpus/manifest.json line 6:
     "url": "https://mft.rrc.texas.gov/link/f11363bb-8120-4e8c-bbc0-a253ec0a85d4",

2. truth/ascii/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   Fields from the RRC Drilling Permit Master daily file.
   Evidence, build_corpus.py line 14:
     truth/ascii/<permit>.json       RRC ASCII master fields (SYSTEM-EXTRACTED, the different hand)
   Evidence, truth/ascii/918133.json line 75:
     "basis": "RRC daf420.dat 2026-09-04, OGA049M positions"

3. truth/w1/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   W-1 form fields and word boxes from the RRC facsimile text layer.
   Evidence, build_corpus.py line 15:
     truth/w1/<permit>.json          W-1 form fields from the facsimile text layer + word boxes (SYSTEM-EXTRACTED)
   Evidence, truth/w1/918133.json line 312:
     "basis": "RRC W-1 facsimile text layer (pdftotext -layout / -bbox-layout); boxes normalized to page",

4. truth/split/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   Page ranges per class, with the RRC file names of each packet.
   Evidence, build_corpus.py line 16:
     truth/split/<permit>.json       true page ranges per class (OBSERVED from packet assembly)

5. truth/classify/*.json (26 files, one per RRC document)
   The class of each RRC document; each file name carries the RRC file name.
   Evidence, build_corpus.py line 17:
     truth/classify/<permit>.json    true class per raw document (OBSERVED from RRC file naming)

6. fixtures/responses/<permit>.json (9 files: 907829, 917176, 917669,
   918133, 918151, 918203, 918233, 918289, 918387)
   Synthetic parser responses generated from the truth files above, so they
   carry RRC values and RRC file names. The fixtures/responses/synth/
   folder is not included here; it is synthetic.
   Evidence, make_fixtures.py line 4:
     Every fixture is derived from truth plus labeled perturbations. The perturbation list is written into each
   Evidence, fixtures/responses/918133.json line 9:
     "file": "918133_W1_AsApprovedW1-9-3-2026_LTR.pdf",

Not shipped
-----------

The RRC permit PDFs (corpus/raw/), the assembled packets (corpus/packets/),
and the permit master daily file are not in this repository.
build_corpus.py rebuilds them from local copies; its source URLs, on
mft.rrc.texas.gov and www.rrc.texas.gov, are at build_corpus.py lines 31-33.

